+            // tracking dropped. The frame is reported as drawn even though it was
+            // not, deliberately: the slot it reserved is half filled, and falling
+            // through to the flat path would hand the caller an eye of that slot
+            // to draw a whole frame into. The surface never publishes a frame
+            // missing an eye, so this costs one frame of the compositor showing
+            // the previous one, and the slot returns to the ring on its own.
+            return true;
